[%# Discovery, alongside the streaming port.  1900/udp is SSDP, which is how
    DLNA clients find the server; 32410/32412/32413/32414/udp is Plex GDM, the
    protocol local servers and clients use to find each other; 32469/udp is
    the DLNA server itself.  Without these a client that already has the
    address can still reach it, but nothing on the LAN can find that address
    in the first place.

    Opened unconditionally rather than behind a flag: a media server nobody can
    find is the failure mode people actually hit, and a flag to turn discovery
    off for someone who does not want GDM and DLNA answering on their LAN is
    easy to add later if anyone asks for one. -%]
[plexmediaserver]
title=Plex Media Server
description=Plex personal media streaming server
ports=32400/tcp|1900,32410,32412,32413,32414,32469/udp
